XDealing with Shapechangers:
X
XOnce you begin to encounter shapechangers, you should already be able
Xto deal with all the other creatures. The shape-changers, however,
are the Xmost potentially dangerous creatures in the game, because
they cannot be Xgenocided and can turn into previously genocided
creatures. X
XREAL SPOILERS:
X
XThe following are spoilers which go beyond (in my opinion) helpful
hints. XSome of these spoilers (in fact most of them) can be figured
out in the Xcourse of play, but they also dramatically change how the
game works. XRead this only if you are truly stuck.
X
XELBERETH:
X
XAny version which has engraving has the secret word Elbereth in it.
XIf the user etches the word "Elbereth" on the ground, and does not
smudge Xthe word by moving (you may type "."), monster will flee in
terror upon Xmoving adjacent to the user, so long as the user stands
on that space. It Xworks much like a scare monster scroll, except
that the user can not attack Xoff of it and preserve its abilities.
X
XUsing Elbereth allows a competent player to win at will, but it is
Xbasically cheating. It is possible to guess about the word Elbereth,
however. XUse it only when no one is watching. Elbereth has been
weakened as of Xrelease 2.2 of NetHack. The various denzins of the
dungeon can throw stuff Xat you and other indirect attacks. You have
a chance of rubbing out the XElbereth unless you use a sharp weapon
or a Magic Marker. X
XEXCALIBUR:
X
XIn nethack, there is a fairly good chance that any long sword named
X"Excalibur" will become +5 after being dipped in a fountain. This
gives a Xvery powerful weapon to anyone who can get a long sword; in
particular a Xknight.
X
XCROESUS:
X
XCroesus is the name that the vault guard is expecting. This does not
Xhelp you win the game, but is listed for the curious.
X
XTHE RUBBER CHICKEN ATTACK:
X
XIf the user is wearing gloves, he may pick up and wield a dead
Xcockatrice. Any creature struck by the bird is automatically turned
to Xstone. Unfortunately, the cockatrice disintigrates after a period
of time, Xbut in the mean time it can wreak vast devastation. Be
careful! Should Xyou fall down while carrying a dead cockatrice, it
may accidentally Xtouch you! The cockatrice, though a powerful
weapon, is not a good Xweapon because it turns potential food into
stone. Just a warning. X
XPOLYMORPHING WANDS:
X
XOne really big spoiler is that should you collect a large number of
Xwands (from a wand shop, for example), and put them in a pile, you
may Xpolymorph the wands, and try to get wands of wishing. With
enough wands and Xcharges in your polymorph wand, you can eventually
get at least one wand of Xwishing. By wishing for more polymorph
wands, you can continue the process, Xacquiring a truly disgusting
number of wishes. The best part is that the Xcharges are the charges
the old wand had, so that one wand may have up Xto 15 wishes!!
Clearly this presents a simple, yet powerful (and cheap) Xmethod of
winning. This is also the only use I have found for the Xfabled "wand
of nothing." They have a lot of charges. X
XPOLYMORPHING YOUR DOG:
X
XIf you want a real powerful pet, you can polymorph your dog, and he
Xwill remain loyal to you. However, if you have a large dog, he's
Xprobably just as good without being polymorphed.
X
XPRAYING FOR FOOD:
X
XOne fairly common effect of praying is that the character is
surrounded Xby a strong aura. This aura not only heals damage and
restores strength, but Xit also raises the user's maximum hp. by 5
AND restores the user's hunger to Xits initial value of 900 turns.
This means that, by praying every 300+ turns, Xeven if this result
only occurs once out of every four tries, the amount Xof food that
needs to be eaten is better than halved. Use the time option Xto keep
track of when it is time to pray. X
